-- title:
--   Hypotheses of the complex uniformisation for Γ(R,ι)
-- statement:
--   Let $q,q'$ be primes, let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$, and assume `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q q'` for the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$: that $0<a$ or $0<b$, and that for every $v$ in the height one spectrum of the ring of integers of $\mathbb{Q}$ the base change $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ has every nonzero element a unit precisely when $q\in v$ or $q'\in v$. Let $R$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which is an order in the sense of `IsOrder`, namely $1\in R$, $R$ is closed under multiplication, the $\mathbb{Q}$-span of $R$ is everything, and $R$ is finitely generated; and let $\iota:\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\to M_2(\mathbb{R})$ be an injective $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra homomorphism. Write $\Gamma=$ `fuchsianGroup R ι` for the subgroup of $GL_2(\mathbb{R})$ obtained by intersecting the image under $\iota$ of the subgroup of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]^{\times}$ generated by the units satisfying the predicate `IsUnitOf R` with the kernel of the determinant. Then: every $\gamma\in\Gamma$ has $\det\gamma=1$; $-1\in\Gamma$; $\Gamma$, as a subspace of $GL_2(\mathbb{R})$, is discrete; and there is a compact subset $K$ of the upper half plane such that every $\tau$ in the upper half plane has some $\gamma\in\Gamma$ with $\gamma\cdot\tau\in K$.
--
--   This packages the four properties of the norm-one unit group of an order in an indefinite rational quaternion division algebra — determinant one, containing $-1$, discrete, and cocompact on the upper half plane — in exactly the form required by the complex uniformisation of the associated Shimura curve. It is used by the construction of the uniformised Hecke curve and of period maps for the quaternionic moduli problem.
